  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d21438f07bf2e8446b0a1da7bf64f675, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day18
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dayNumber: 18
  storyText: "We started talking about food today. Not the instant noodles we've
    been eating for almost three weeks. Real food. Someone mentioned pho. The smell
    of broth in the morning, lime on the side, chili floating on top. Another person
    said banh mi \u2014 crispy bread, p\xE2t\xE9, that little thrill when you bite
    into a hidden piece of pork. Someone else just whispered \"fried rice.\" We all
    went quiet. We used to complain about the canteen food. Too oily. Too plain.
    Same thing every day. Now? We'd kill for a plate of that terrible fried rice.
    We'd kill for anything that isn't in a plastic wrapper. The ducks outside are
    eating worms. Even they eat better than us now.\r"
